# Descriptions distinguish source-integrity guarantees from model quality claims.
SECTIONS = [
("1. Project purpose and delivery boundaries", [
("1.1 GSME Muse use case", "GSME Muse is a document-grounded assistant for Muse FAQs, tapeout-related information, semiconductor concepts and manufacturing documents. The corpus is not restricted to short FAQ pairs: it includes paragraph-style explanations, numbered technical sections, tables, slides, spreadsheets and image-bearing PDFs. The intended answer is a concise explanation with source extracts and document links. When accepted evidence does not support the question, the application must state that limitation instead of filling the gap with general model knowledge."),
("1.2 What has been built", "The repository implements parsing into normalized Markdown, structural and optional local semantic chunking, evidence diagnostics, separate review decisions, versioned relational storage, approved-evidence embedding jobs, a Qdrant-derived index, dense and hybrid candidate search, mandatory reranking for generated answers, bounded answer generation, structured schedule search and a browser chatbot. It also includes a loopback operator console, offline evaluation utilities and regression tests. Implementation does not mean every document has completed indexing or that all model outputs have been independently source-verified."),
("1.3 Explicit limitations", "This handover is not a claim of perfect retrieval or production certification. OCR can misread characters; selectable PDF text can be mathematically wrong; table inference can drop cells; API quotas can stop embedding, reranking or generation. Google sign-in needs real company OAuth configuration, and company hosting needs persistent services, HTTPS, backups and operational ownership. The existing deployment descriptor is a demo scaffold, not proof that the new hosted chatbot is deployed correctly."),
("1.4 Documentation evidence", "Descriptions are based on the checked-out Python modules, SQL migrations, browser code, local source inspection and the verification results recorded in this document. Older conversation reports of live evaluations are not restated as current measurements. The repository README has been corrected to describe GSME setup, trust boundaries, updates and deployment limitations. Source-specific evaluation artifacts remain local under ignored validation/ rather than being published with company extracts."),
]),
("2. System architecture and end-to-end flows", [
("2.1 Main components", "The Python package separates parsing, chunking, storage, retrieval, generation and hosted access. FastAPI serves the chatbot and API endpoints. PostgreSQL owns source versions, current publication pointers, evidence status, review decisions, ingestion/index jobs, schedule records and chat history. Qdrant stores derived vectors and lexical-search payloads. Original files and normalized artifacts live below the configured data directory. Cohere supplies the current external embedding and reranking adapters; Cohere Command or optionally Gemini supplies primary answers; Ollama is an optional local answer fallback."),
("2.2 Ingestion lifecycle", "The upload endpoint validates identity or browser workspace, request origin, file size and allowed format. It copies and hashes the original into version-specific storage, creates an ingestion job and assigns owner-only access. The worker claims a leased job, records the local parsing profile, parses to Markdown, chunks the result and retains the manifest and diagnostics. Clean ordinary prose can pass a conservative automatic policy. Uncertain evidence stays held. Publication and indexing are separate states: accepted text is not searchable as a vector until the matching index job completes."),
("2.3 Question lifecycle", "A question is scoped to the server-configured tenant, current principal and optional document. The database first computes eligible indexed point IDs. The application embeds the query, searches dense vectors and optionally BM25 lexical evidence, fuses candidates, rechecks their relational eligibility, sends a bounded candidate list to the reranker and assembles context. Generation can use only current accepted context. The server validates citation identities, exact source excerpts and unsupported numeric values/URLs, then groups only used citations for display. Access is checked again before the response leaves the server."),
("2.4 Structured schedule lifecycle", "Schedule records are parsed and stored as typed rows rather than treated only as prose embeddings. Search uses explicit Full/Shared kind, technology, flavor, milestone field, dates and timezone, with deterministic filtering and version snapshots. The hosted Tapeout schedules switch calls the dedicated access-filtered schedule API. Document chat does not guess schedule intent from words such as GDS. Schedule lookups remain separate from saved chat turns and do not call an embedding, reranking or answer model."),
("2.5 Trust boundaries", "A source document, user question or model response is data, not an instruction source for the application. Browser bodies cannot choose tenant, owner, reviewer or publication visibility. Qdrant payloads cannot grant source access or approval. An HTTP 200 conversion is not a source-fidelity certificate. A model quote that appears verbatim in a document is not, by itself, proof that the quote logically supports the generated claim."),
]),
("3. Document parsing and normalization", [
("3.1 Parser contract", "parsing/parser.py dispatches by extension and returns ParsedDocument: filename, document_type, strategy_used, Markdown, warnings, metadata and evidence diagnostics. The source is hashed before and after parsing so a file changed during extraction cannot be attributed to an earlier digest. DocumentMetadata records original and normalized SHA-256 digests, source identity, document class, schedule classification and parser version. The exact strategy_used field identifies the actual backend; a fallback result must never be reported as a successful Docling conversion."),
("3.2 Native PDF processing", "The PyMuPDF path reads text spans, positions, font sizes, bold share and source block order. It identifies headings and paragraph units, handles supported FAQ-table layouts and supplements relevant raster regions with local OCR. Repeated text is removed only when repetition and top/bottom page position support a page-furniture classification. A document number appearing in a genuine body paragraph is not automatically removed. Landscape presentation pages can isolate their heading context so an unrelated slide title does not become a heading for later pages."),
("3.3 Optional Docling processing", "The optional PDF dependency set pins Docling and its table-model package together because table-cell diagnostics depend on an internal matcher contract. Docling conversion uses structural items and provenance to recover page position, text, tables and pictures. The wrapper retains raw evidence when the table matcher drops cells and issues a source-located warning where location can be established. If dropped cells cannot be uniquely matched to a page, that uncertainty is explicit. No alternate extraction is declared superior merely because its Markdown looks cleaner."),
("3.4 OCR prerequisites and provenance", "The same parser process must see a usable Tesseract executable and English language data. The source profile records availability; an executable visible only in a different shell does not establish parser readiness. OCR is used for relevant raster evidence and targeted technical-text diagnostics. OCR output remains review-marked. An A17/Al7 disagreement is preserved as an alternate reading, not silently reconciled by assuming a familiar identifier. Confidence scores or a plausible word are not independent source verification."),
("3.5 Word FAQ parsing", "DOCX processing uses python-docx and document XML structures to read paragraphs, heading/bold-question patterns, answers, tables and supported hyperlinks. A bold paragraph that is a real FAQ question can anchor the following answer; incidental question marks in technical prose must not reclassify an entire document as an FAQ. Table-based question and answer columns preserve the relationship between a question and its answer. Category rows are not invented as answer cells."),
("3.6 PowerPoint and Excel", "PPTX parsing uses python-pptx; XLSX parsing uses openpyxl. They have local synthetic regression coverage, but user-provided production PPTX/XLSX examples still require representative acceptance review. Extraction does not execute macros or spreadsheet formulas. Images, charts, merged cells and formula-dependent values can require review. A text preview is explicitly an extracted preview, not an assurance that the original Office layout was reproduced. Legacy binary DOC/PPT/XLS files are not in the supported extension list."),
("3.7 CSV and schedule recognition", "CSV is read as structured rows with source-row attribution. Header recognition, not an arbitrary filename alone, determines whether it has schedule shape. Full/Shared classification can derive from an explicit supported context or recognized source naming; ambiguous classification is surfaced. An XLSX schedule workbook can derive kinds from worksheets. Typed dates and technology fields are validated rather than supplied by an LLM."),
("3.8 Hyperlinks", "A source hyperlink target is retained where the file format exposes it. Text such as 'here' without a usable destination generates link_target_missing. The application must not guess a URL from the surrounding topic. Downstream chunks need both the source wording and the real link target; otherwise that claimed destination remains unavailable. This is particularly relevant to Shared Block schedule FAQ answers that visually appear to contain a link."),
("3.9 Control markers and Markdown integrity", "Normalization puts each page, review and section marker on its own line so parsing does not join it to ordinary text. Review start/end markers scope uncertainty. Page markers drive page attribution, and isolated-page markers reset unsuitable inherited context. The normalized Markdown digest is recorded at ingestion. Reading an artifact verifies the digest; a deliberately narrow legacy CRLF/LF recovery is allowed only if it reproduces the already recorded hash. Real content edits require a new version."),
]),
("4. Evidence fidelity and visual review", [
("4.1 Diagnostic record", "EvidenceDiagnostic preserves a stable evidence ID, document digest, type, source page, bounding box, original selectable text, alternate OCR reading and reason. Coordinates refer to the source-page region, not a guessed semantic location. Raw technical text is retained for inspection. Review decisions are separate from extraction artifacts so accepting, rejecting or excluding an item does not rewrite the original observation."),
("4.2 Broken fonts and technical text", "The local detector checks replacement characters, private-use Unicode ranges, unmapped CID tokens, incomplete operators and suspicious mathematical layout. It renders only a bounded set of suspicious regions for alternate OCR, avoiding a full OCR pass over every selectable-text page. Disagreement is diagnostic, not a license to rewrite values, dates, units, code or formulas. A broken symbol can change technical meaning even when most of the sentence is readable."),
("4.3 Formula safeguards", "A selectable equation is not necessarily a correct linear transcription. Fractions, denominators, superscripts and symbol position may be lost. The manual regression cases include the page 30 DPPM equation and page 163 control-chart/yield expressions. The safe representation preserves source location and holds suspect text until source review supplies a verified transcription. The application does not infer missing algebra to make a formula appear complete."),
("4.4 Tables and dropped cells", "Docling-inferred tables and uncertain PDF cell reconstruction are review-gated. A matcher warning about unmatched cells is potential data loss, not a harmless log line. Raw cell text, grid dimensions, cell identities and table/page locations are retained where available. Numeric and merged tables require row/header comparison against the original. A table cell that fails matching may contain data; the correct response is inspection and coverage analysis, not suppressing the warning."),
("4.5 Charts, figures and OCR ordering", "Recovered chart labels can be retained with review status without claiming that text order proves a category-to-percentage mapping. The page 101 manual chart is an example: extracted percentages do not verify their visual associations. Figure captions are deduplicated conservatively. Raster OCR is placed at source/figure context where possible and must not become a document heading or inherit an unrelated later numbered section. Logos and repeated decorative assets are distinguished from substantive unverified diagrams where supported by source analysis."),
("4.6 Visual placeholders", "A generic sentence such as 'Visual evidence on page ... requires source review' is a diagnostic placeholder, not useful verified semantic evidence. Such units are excluded from embedding. Their page/region remains inspectable by an operator. A future chart description or vision-model output still needs the configured permission gate and separate evidence review; a generated description is not automatically promoted to an approved claim."),
]),
("5. Chunking design and metadata", [
("5.1 Structural units", "chunking/chunker.py reads normalized Markdown into blocks and source units. It recognizes headings, FAQ question/answer pairs, table rows, paragraphs, fenced code and control markers. The automatic route selects suitable structural handling for FAQ-like, paper-like and general documents. A heading path is context, not a source of new factual assertions. Numbered section hierarchy is preserved only when the source supports it; OCR image text is not promoted to a section title."),
("5.2 FAQ preservation", "A question and its answer are kept together as a meaningful retrieval unit where possible. The original question is recorded in faq_question only for recognized FAQ chunks; it is not inferred for every paragraph ending in a question mark. Table FAQ rows are serialized with explicit Question and Answer meaning rather than losing column labels. Incidental questions should retain their true section context instead of inheriting the heading of a preceding table."),
("5.3 Size limits and intact evidence", "The normal character target is 1,800 characters. This is a segmentation target, not permission to truncate an indivisible record. Long source units can carry unit_id, part_index and part_count. Complete-part reconstruction is required before generation uses a split unit. Intact oversized rows preserve column meaning and require explicit warning/review handling. Embedding token limits, rerank byte limits and generation prompt limits are separate constraints; satisfying one does not imply the others are satisfied."),
("5.4 Contextual chunking", "Chunks carry source file, category, heading path, page start/end and optional row numbers, so isolated text retains its source context. There is no hidden LLM-generated contextual preamble that becomes trusted original evidence. Query-time same-unit reconstruction restores long approved units. The new explicit-comparison expansion can add up to three approved prose siblings from the same comparison heading near the retrieved anchor, preserving independent source identities. Those siblings are contextual source evidence, not additional reranked vector hits."),
("5.5 Optional semantic boundaries", "The semantic strategy calls local Ollama nomic-embed-text only to compare paragraph-level topic boundaries. It does not replace Cohere document embeddings in the search collection. The local model digest is recorded in the ingestion profile, and a changed or missing digest fails rather than silently changing version identity. Input is bounded to 512 paragraph segments. The splitter verifies that concatenating the proposed pieces exactly reproduces the original text."),
("5.6 Chunk identity", "A chunk record includes stable source/chunk IDs, chunk index/type, content digest, source anchor, heading path, category, page/row attribution, split-unit metadata, parser/chunker versions, review_required and evidence status. The same text in a different source or parser profile is not assumed to have identical provenance. Character count is derived from text. Serialization omits absent optional fields but does not remove a true review flag."),
]),
("6. Review and acceptance policy", [
("6.1 Clean text versus human verification", "automatic_clean_text_v1 accepts only supported ordinary text units that pass conservative checks. It records source_verified=false and an automatic policy basis; it does not claim a human read the source. True source review uses a separately authorized reviewer, rationale and source verification. Review-required extraction, broken characters, formulas, OCR text and missing hyperlink destinations cannot be approved merely to complete an upload progress bar."),
("6.2 Warning scope", "Known image/table/figure warnings can be scoped to their marked extraction units. A table warning elsewhere on a page must not indefinitely block clean selectable prose above it. Unknown or genuinely page-wide fidelity warnings remain blocking. Both Python acceptance logic and SQL eligibility functions implement this distinction. Raw warnings remain retained even where their effective scope does not block a particular paragraph."),
("6.3 Append-only decisions", "Review decisions are separate records with chunk identity, decision, verification state, reviewer, rationale, approval basis and time/order. The latest valid decision participates in the approved-current-evidence view. Rejecting or revoking evidence removes its eligibility immediately at the relational boundary, even if stale Qdrant vectors have not yet been reconciled away. Reconciliation cleans the derived index; it is not the primary access-control mechanism."),
("6.4 Review rationale", "A rationale explains what was checked and why evidence was accepted or rejected, for example that a merged table row was compared with the original page. It is not intended as a repeated manual step for every clean FAQ paragraph. The chatbot performs clean-text acceptance automatically where safe; the local operator console handles the genuinely uncertain subset. Removing review flags to reduce clicks would obscure evidence risk rather than resolve it."),
]),
("7. PostgreSQL storage and document versioning", [
("7.1 Relational authority", "documents identifies a tenant-scoped document and current version. document_versions records immutable source/artifact references, parser and chunker versions, source profile and lifecycle state. evidence_chunks stores normalized evidence and provenance. review_decisions governs approval. ingestion_jobs and index_jobs track durable work. document_access stores ownership/publication policies. Schedule tables store typed imported records. Hosted chat/session/request-limit tables provide the browser application layer."),
("7.2 Version identity and incremental work", "Submission checks source identity and extraction profile so the same unchanged input does not unnecessarily become an indistinguishable duplicate. A changed parser, chunker, backend or local semantic-model digest can legitimately require a new parse version. Index jobs use deterministic point identities and model-version separation. Identical approved text can reuse a compatible stored vector in the same tenant/model/collection, but reuse never transfers an old source's approval to a new source."),
("7.3 Artifact layout", "GSME_DATA_DIR defaults to ./data. Originals are stored below originals/<hashed-tenant>/<version>/source.<extension>. Artifacts are version/attempt specific and include normalized Markdown plus parse/chunk/manifest material written by the pipeline. The filename displayed in the interface is source metadata, not a browser-accessible filesystem URL. Opening a source passes through the authorized application endpoint."),
("7.4 Migration management", "Numbered SQL migrations are packaged with the Python distribution. EvidenceStore.migrate serializes migrations with a PostgreSQL advisory lock and records applied names in schema_migrations. The local hosted launcher migrates before serving. A managed factory deployment must run migrations explicitly. Migration 011 adds automatic-upload continuation fields; migration 012 adds owner-scoped chat threads and turns. Additive schema migration does not substitute for database backup and restore testing."),
("7.5 Publication and availability", "Only current published approved evidence participates in normal retrieval. Publication changes a document's current pointer, and superseded versions are filtered out. This is a correctness safeguard, but updates are not claimed to be zero-downtime blue/green index swaps: a new current version that is still indexing may have reduced search coverage. That limitation requires deliberate operational handling before a production SLA is promised."),
("7.6 Deletion semantics", "The browser Delete action revokes an owner's private upload from chat/search, cancels automatic work and supersedes relevant versions/jobs; its confirmation states that originals/audit evidence remain for recovery. Required documents can be protected from deletion. Shared library files are operator-managed. This differs from an explicitly authorized permanent purge, which must separately account for SQL records, vector points, originals, artifacts and retained operational logs."),
]),
("8. Embeddings and Qdrant index", [
("8.1 Embedding adapter", "The current Cohere adapter uses embed-v5.0-pro with search_document for accepted document text, and embed-v5.0-fast with search_query for questions. Its stored model identity describes this configured retrieval pairing; it does not mean each stage calls the same endpoint model. The configured output dimension defaults to 1,024. Changing the document model or retrieval pairing requires compatibility checks and model/collection identity handling, not simply substituting vectors in an existing index. The local fake adapter is test-only and is isolated from real evidence-answer claims."),
("8.2 Token and input validation", "Before embedding, text is checked against the provider token budget without silent truncation. The default embedding ceiling is 8,192 tokens, with bounded application batches. An over-budget source is not embedded as a cut-off technical claim. Provider vectors are validated for expected dimension, finite numeric values and nonzero magnitude. Collection dimension/cosine configuration is checked before writing vectors."),
("8.3 Physical storage", "Embedding coordinates are stored in Qdrant, not inside the browser and not in the original PDF. PostgreSQL stores the chunk/job/model/point identity needed to find them. The default real collection is gsme_evidence_v1; synthetic tests use separate synthetic or uniquely named integration collections. With Docker Compose, Qdrant persists in its named Docker volume and PostgreSQL in a separate named volume. Deleting a container is different from deleting its persistent volume."),
("8.4 Payloads and hybrid lexical features", "Qdrant payloads include source/tenant/model identity, text digest and accepted text needed for candidate search and compatible-vector reuse. They are derived data. Hybrid operation installs the lexical text index with BM25 scoring and combines lexical/dense candidates. The application does not trust a payload's approval or owner label in place of the current PostgreSQL join. Optional CLI indexing configuration and the hosted retrieval strategy should be inspected separately: a single GSME_HYBRID flag does not describe every call site."),
("8.5 Job safety", "Leases and heartbeats detect stale workers. Approval/current-version locks protect a bounded embedding batch against concurrent source changes. A successful external request is not enough: the corresponding relational job must be recorded, and interrupted indexing must be recoverable without repeatedly publishing the same version. Missing or stale vectors can be repaired/reconciled from authoritative records. Vector reuse requires matching text hash and valid stored payload/vector, not approximate semantic similarity."),
("8.6 What vector previews mean", "The operator embedding preview exposes model version, collection, point ID, dimension, norm and a small coordinate sample for an approved indexed chunk. A 404 saying no current approved indexed vector may mean the chunk is not approved, not yet indexed, superseded or requested under the wrong provider/model collection. A vector sample demonstrates storage, not semantic correctness or how well a query will retrieve that chunk."),
]),
("9. Automatic background ingestion and provider failures", [
("9.1 No repeated manual Retry for transient limits", "Hosted uploads enroll durable automatic work. The server scheduler polls due work and advances bounded batches independently of browser polling. next-attempt time, retry count and safe error codes survive a browser close and server restart. Per-version advisory locking and process-level slots prevent duplicate workers from advancing the same upload concurrently. A document larger than one processing slice can continue through later slices automatically."),
("9.2 Backoff versus permanent blocks", "A retryable rate limit or transport problem uses bounded retries and an appropriate cooldown. Monthly quota exhaustion, invalid credentials, missing content approval and unresolved source review are not treated as transient success. They stop with an actionable status rather than retrying forever. Existing indexed passages remain eligible during a partial-ingestion cooldown, but questions still depend on available query-embedding, reranking and answer-provider quota."),
("9.3 Quota diagnosis", "Token usage shown in a provider dashboard is not the same as an API-call allowance. Tokenization requests and retries can consume request quota too. Earlier provider responses identified an exhausted monthly API-call allowance; a new key for the same quota scope is not assumed to create new capacity. The code classifies quota errors separately from short rate limits. The precise reset time belongs to the provider account and cannot be restored by application code."),
("9.4 Tokenization cache", "Successful exact tokenizations are cached in bounded process memory, keyed by credential namespace, model and text hash. Failed responses and guessed token counts are not cached as valid measurements. This reduces duplicate calls without bypassing the provider's actual token budget. It is not a durable cross-process quota cache, and a server restart may require tokenizing again."),
("9.5 Fairness and performance limits", "Upload and chat concurrency are bounded separately. Progress messages explain parsing, embedding, cooldown and operator-attention states. Local availability does not guarantee that background ingestion cannot affect foreground API quota or latency. CPU-heavy layout conversion and OCR also share machine resources. Production fairness needs measured capacity, queue observability and potentially a separate worker service, rather than assuming a thread pool guarantees isolation."),
]),
("10. Retrieval, hybrid fusion and query planning", [
("10.1 Eligibility before similarity", "Before vector search, retrieval_scope selects current approved indexed points matching tenant, access policy, model, collection and optional source/category filters. This eligible point set is passed into the vector query, preventing a narrow document search from being crowded out by inaccessible or irrelevant top hits from the wider corpus. Results are rejoined through allowed_hits before reranking, then rechecked after provider calls."),
("10.2 Dense and hybrid strategies", "Dense search ranks vector similarity. Hybrid adds lexical BM25 evidence, useful for acronyms, technical identifiers and rare exact terms that dense search can underweight. Rank fusion combines ranking signals rather than treating incompatible raw scores as probabilities. RetrievalOptions defaults to hybrid, candidate_count=30 and top_k=5. Values are bounded: top_k 1–20, candidate count at least top_k and at most 100, and a separate context character budget."),
("10.3 Query rewriting and multi-query", "Planning is conservative and local. The original question is preserved, including negation, dates, units and identifiers. Opt-in expanded mode appends known domain acronym hints; multi mode adds bounded query variants with deduplication and rank fusion. At most three variants are generated. The hosted chat currently uses the default original query mode, so it would be inaccurate to claim that every chatbot question already gets LLM rewriting or multi-query retrieval."),
("10.4 Routing decisions", "Query-planning code includes document/schedule planning for explicit operations and evaluation. Hosted Chat searches documents to avoid misrouting FAQ questions about GDS deadlines into an exact schedule parser. Greetings have a small literal local response path. The Chat / Tapeout schedules switch makes the choice explicit. Schedule questions use a bounded local grammar plus optional milestone/date filters, not automatic LLM intent routing. Conflicting wording and selected filters request clarification."),
("10.5 Context assembly and deduplication", "The service deduplicates repeated point IDs, source units and duplicate evidence text before constructing final context. Split units are reassembled only from eligible current parts; missing parts make the unit incomplete and unsuitable for complete-evidence generation. Whole passages that exceed context budgets are omitted with warnings rather than silently cut. Equal-score ranking receives a stable identity tie-break so incidental ordering does not shuffle prompts unnecessarily."),
("10.6 Cross-page comparisons", "The fabless/IDM defect showed that a relevant anchor can land on page 27 while the definition of the second entity starts on page 28. A narrowly bounded section expansion now activates only for an explicit comparison question and a comparison heading among the first two results. It selects same-version, same-heading approved ordinary prose within six chunk positions and one page either side, excludes review-required/table/split evidence, and adds at most three siblings within the context budget. These sibling passages do not require new vector embeddings, but their approval and access are rechecked. Diagnostics mark them as approved section context, not as extra reranked candidates."),
]),
("11. Cross-encoder reranking", [
("11.1 Process", "The reranker receives the original question and the bounded candidate passage texts. It jointly evaluates question/passage relevance and returns a score/index for each candidate. The application validates indices, uniqueness, completeness and finite scores before using the ranking. Default hosted retrieval sends at most 30 candidates for one question, not every chunk in the corpus. top_k=5 describes the selected result units, not the total number of passages transmitted to rerank."),
("11.2 Model and thresholds", "The configured default is rerank-v5.0-pro, with supported fast/pro model choices constrained by application validation. Timeout defaults to 30 seconds and the conservative rerank input guard to 8,192 UTF-8 bytes. GSME_MIN_RERANK_SCORE is unset by default pending verified calibration. A relevance score is not a probability that an answer is true. Picking an arbitrary score threshold such as 0.5 without a labeled corpus can discard correct evidence or retain near-topic negatives."),
("11.3 Mandatory reranking boundary", "Generated answers require completed reranking. If query embedding or reranking fails, the application does not present an unreranked generation as an equivalent result. Operational error messages distinguish quota, cooldown, configuration and ranking-stage failure. Ollama answer fallback cannot repair a missing query embedding or a failed mandatory reranker because the source-selection stage has not successfully completed."),
("11.4 Evaluation", "Benchmarking records the expected passage's candidate rank, reranked rank and final-context position, plus score and top-1/top-3/top-5/top-10 hit indicators. MRR captures how early the first expected match appears. A rank change shows whether reranking helped a particular case; an aggregate hit rate does not establish that the final answer used the right passage or preserved conditions. Near-topic negative questions need separate answer-abstention evaluation."),
]),
("12. Answer generation, fallback and source display", [
("12.1 Primary model adapters", "The answer settings support Cohere Command as the default or an optional Gemini adapter when its model/key and separate content approval are configured. The default Command setting is command-a-plus-05-2026; this is a configuration value, not a claim of permanent provider availability. Gemini selection changes answer generation, not the Cohere embedding or reranking stages. A fully Cohere-independent system would need a compatible replacement reranker and a separately migrated embedding index. Primary selection is configuration-driven: this implementation is not presented as an automatic small-model/large-model complexity router."),
("12.2 Ollama fallback", "Ollama qwen3:4b is the configured local answer fallback. It is used for operational primary-provider unavailability, not to overrule a model's valid insufficient-evidence decision or to bypass a failed citation/schema check. It must be installed and reachable locally. A small local model can differ in instruction following and generation quality; the repository does not claim it matches a larger hosted model. Fallback cannot create evidence absent from the documents."),
("12.3 Structured generation protocol", "The model receives a bounded evidence list and a JSON schema. Each evidence item has a server-issued quote ID. The model selects IDs rather than retyping a supposedly exact supporting quote, and the server copies the actual source text. The schema limits claim count and claim size. The system prompt forbids invented URLs, dates, formulas and chart mappings, source-instruction following and unsupported company facts. Temperature is zero for improved repeatability, not a guarantee of identical or correct output."),
("12.4 Local validation", "Validation checks parseable structured output, status/claim consistency, known source IDs, exact support text membership and numeric/URL coverage in cited text. Duplicate JSON fields are rejected. Source access is checked again after model completion. These are useful integrity controls, not a universal semantic entailment engine. The fabless/IDM guard rejects claims citing only a model-name introduction for an IDM property. Hosted Fabless-vs-IDP queries explicitly disclose a conditional IDM interpretation, preserve the original question and allow the user to correct the meaning. Other acronyms are not generally autocorrected."),
("12.5 Compression and prompt budgets", "Optional paragraph compression selects exact source paragraphs and records excerpt spans; it does not ask an LLM to rewrite evidence. The default is no compression. The shared answer prompt budget is conservatively bounded at 6,000 bytes and output at 1,024 tokens, with model-specific reasoning allowance where implemented. If complete passages cannot fit, they are omitted with a warning. Retrieval top_k and final generation evidence count can therefore differ."),
("12.6 Stability and answer cache", "A short-lived bounded in-memory cache reuses a previously validated primary answer only for the exact question, owner/workspace/document scope, model/settings and identical evidence snapshot. Source ordering is canonicalized before assigning E1/E2 labels. Context and answer fingerprints expose whether two replies used the same evidence and validated claims. Retrieval still runs freshly before reuse, and access is checked on a cache hit. The cache does not fix an incorrect first answer or restore API quota."),
("12.7 Citation presentation", "Only actually cited validated quotations become answer source cards. Identical quotes are folded while preserving their source references; multiple passages from one original are grouped under that document. [E1], [E2] and similar buttons expand the matching source passage, and Open document opens its authorized preview. Search matches shown after abstention are explicitly labeled as not used in an answer. They must not be mistaken for support for a generated statement."),
("12.8 Streaming without bypassing validation", "The hosted streaming endpoint consumes actual Cohere content deltas, Gemini SSE content or Ollama NDJSON. It incrementally parses structured output and emits only complete claims after source-ID, exact-support, numeric/URL and current-access checks. Access is checked again before dequeued claims and final results are transmitted, so a queued item cannot bypass later revocation. Raw partial JSON, model thinking and unvalidated claims are not displayed. A visible reply is provisional until final schema/status/access checks complete; invalid endings, source revocation and interrupted connections discard the draft. Cache hits may finish immediately, without a fake typing animation. This is claim-by-claim streaming, not character-level release of unchecked model text."),
("12.9 Unnecessary comparison clarification", "For a basic explicit fabless/IDM comparison, if both approved source definitions are in the bounded prompt but the model still asks for clarification, the application can return up to two contiguous source-sentence extracts from each definition. It labels the answer protocol verbatim_comparison_extracts_v1 and provider source_extracts. No new contrast or inferred fact is generated. Questions adding constraints such as costs in a particular year do not qualify. A truly ambiguous topic still receives a clarification, but the message does not imply that selecting a file is mandatory when All files can search the collection."),
("12.10 Manufacturing-stage scopes", "The saved question asking for the three main semiconductor manufacturing stages correctly retrieved MFG-GSME-0002 page 18 at rank one and the manufacturing presentation page 11 at rank two. Their scopes differ: manufacturing operations versus stages before market readiness. Version 0.19.11 instructs generation to explain each source scope separately. If a basic three-stage listing still receives model clarification, a narrow local recovery copies complete explicit three-item source sentences, preserving separate citations rather than inventing a combined sequence. It records verbatim_stage_extracts_v1 and a content-free clarification-recovered log event. Stage values are not hard-coded. Extra query constraints, uncertain OCR/table passages, incomplete lists, same-scope conflicts, model insufficiency and revoked evidence are not overridden. This recovery is tested with JSON, streaming, the hosted answer handler and a local replay of the actual saved request. It does not require another provider call or re-embedding; a local replay is not described as a new live Cohere validation."),
]),
("13. Exact tapeout schedule search", [
("13.1 Supported constraints", "ScheduleQuery supports Full, Shared or both kinds; technology in nm; exact flavor; trial, final, tapeout or estimated-ship date; inclusive date range; open/closed status; next-date count; timezone; as-of date; limit/offset and snapshot. Ambiguous natural-language constraints produce clarification rather than broadening SQL. Explicit typed filters cannot silently contradict the words of the question."),
("13.2 Temporal correctness", "Relative dates use an explicit IANA timezone, default Asia/Karachi. The as-of date is returned so a demo can explain why a deadline counts as open or closed. Date-range order is validated. Estimated shipping is not a guaranteed capacity commitment. Imported records have source version/row provenance; the system does not claim to have fetched current live foundry capacity just because a schedule row exists."),
("13.3 Consistent paging and source access", "Pagination with an offset requires the previous snapshot, preventing silent mixing of results across schedule updates. A changed source snapshot is a detectable condition. Public schedule rows can be exposed without granting download access to an entire private workbook; source links are omitted when the caller lacks that permission. Exact filtering happens before count/ranking/pagination, not after inaccessible rows have influenced results."),
("13.4 FAQ schedule links versus date lookup", "A FAQ asking where to find a schedule can be answered from a real retained hyperlink. A question asking for imported tapeout dates uses the schedule service. A GDS preliminary/final upload deadline FAQ may be a prose relative-deadline rule, not a calendar lookup. These are different evidence needs. No source destination or calendar date should be inferred from the order of related passages."),
]),
("14. Hosted chatbot, sidebar and chat history", [
("14.1 Interface behaviour", "The browser UI has a document sidebar, source previews, an independent scrollable conversation, a fixed composer, an All files selector and a plus-button upload. Enter sends and Shift+Enter inserts a new line, with IME composition protected. Long responses reveal their beginning rather than forcing the user past the opening text. Reading an older message does not automatically force a scroll to the bottom; Latest messages restores following behaviour."),
("14.2 Collapsible navigation and branding", "The sidebar can now be collapsed or reopened on desktop and uses a modal drawer on small screens. The open state is exposed through aria-expanded, controls have accessible labels and focus is returned to the toggle on close. Only the harmless desktop-collapse preference is saved in browser localStorage. Muse is displayed as a wordmark in place of the former standalone italic m. An official image logo was not supplied, so this is not represented as an approved brand asset."),
("14.3 Multiple conversations", "Chats are stored in PostgreSQL per server-derived tenant and owner subject. New chat starts a separate thread without deleting documents. Conversations can be selected, reopened, renamed and permanently deleted independently of source files. The first saved question supplies a bounded initial title. The current limits are 100 chats per owner and 100 turns per chat. Threads save server-produced replies, not arbitrary browser-supplied citations. Earlier transient UI conversations were not persisted by the old application and cannot be recovered as historical threads."),
("14.4 History privacy", "A browser guest owns history through its opaque workspace cookie; a signed-in user owns it through verified identity. Another browser/user cannot fetch a thread merely by learning its UUID. An anonymous FAQ-only session without a subject can still ask public questions but cannot persist history. Loading history rechecks every source reference and masks an old reply if its evidence has changed or access was revoked. Identity changes discard late requests so private content cannot repopulate the public view."),
("14.5 History is not conversational query rewriting", "Saved chat history provides organization and persistence. It does not make pronouns such as 'what about that one?' automatically resolve to an earlier question. The UI explicitly says questions are searched independently. The API does not send the full saved conversation to an LLM for every turn. This separation bounds cost and prevents old irrelevant text from silently overriding fresh source selection."),
("14.6 Document management", "The sidebar lists authorized filenames with simple processing states instead of searchable-passage counts. Owners can retry eligible interrupted uploads and remove permitted private uploads; shared files are operator-managed. Progress polling is informational: durable server jobs drive processing. PDF/image originals open inline; Office files use a labeled extracted-text preview rather than sending private originals to an external document viewer. Blob URLs are revoked when closing a preview."),
("14.7 Streaming controls and source help", "The interface shows search/generation progress, displays evidence-checked provisional claims and replaces them with the finalized answer and clickable source cards. Stop cancels delivery and removes the unfinished draft. A provider call already blocked in SDK I/O may take until the next read/timeout boundary to stop; its server slot stays held meanwhile to prevent unbounded abandoned work. The compact Upload & source help panel explains automatic ingestion, Ready to chat, All files, filename previews and operator review. The current SSE client handles split UTF-8 characters, CRLF frames, keep-alives, safe error events and incomplete EOF without leaving an unfinished reply visible."),
]),
("15. Security, external approvals and company deployment", [
("15.1 Public FAQs and private uploads", "Explicitly published FAQ versions can be public without sign-in. Private uploads remain owner-only. Temporary no-login testing uses browser workspaces rather than making every upload public. Cookie expiry or clearing cookies loses access to that browser workspace; it does not automatically erase the stored files. This guest mode is convenient for local demonstration but is not a substitute for a company identity lifecycle."),
("15.2 Company identity", "The optional Google Workspace adapter verifies signed token issuer, audience, verified email, allowed hosted domain and stable subject. A company OAuth web client ID and approved domains are still required before real company sign-in is active. Client-selected identities are not trusted. The local operator console is a different trust boundary and should never be exposed publicly as the company chatbot."),
("15.3 Request protections", "Hosted settings validate the application origin and use trusted-host handling. Mutating browser calls use the same-origin session/CSRF boundary. Uploads have a 20 MiB cap and extension validation; public request rates and concurrency are bounded. Error responses attach correlation IDs while avoiding raw provider payloads or API keys. HTTPS and a correctly configured reverse proxy are required off the local machine."),
("15.4 External processing consent", "Embedding, reranking, answer generation, Gemini and visual analysis have distinct content-approval settings. Reranking sends the user question as well as accepted passages. An approval flag is an organizational control, not evidence that a model is accurate. Real keys/passwords/reviewer tokens stay in local secrets or host-managed secrets, never in the example file, DOCX or source control. Existing .env entries should be edited, not duplicated at the bottom."),
("15.5 Hosting readiness", "The local hosted entry point binds loopback on port 8020. A real company deployment needs an externally reachable reverse proxy or suitable application server binding, managed PostgreSQL/Qdrant, persistent artifact storage, secret injection, migrations, HTTPS origins and worker lifecycle management. The existing Render demo configuration points to a demo health path and is not a verified deployment of the current chatbot. A Python/stateful-worker backend cannot be assumed to work unchanged as a purely static Vercel site."),
("15.6 Operational decisions still needed", "Confirm who can publish shared sources, the Google Workspace configuration, the production domain, content retention/deletion policy, database/vector/artifact backups, restore drills, API budget and quota tier, upload limits and monitoring ownership. Also decide how long history should be retained after an employee leaves. The current chat DELETE physically removes that thread and its turns; document DELETE has different recovery-oriented semantics."),
]),
("16. Logging, diagnosis and performance", [
("16.1 Finding the logs", "The local launcher prints the operation-log path, normally data/logs/console.log. Structured events share a request ID across hosted HTTP handling, query embedding, candidate search, reranking, context selection and answer generation. The browser Request details provides the request ID and important answer metadata. Match the UI's identifier with the log to distinguish a search failure from a model abstention."),
("16.2 Safe observability", "The logger uses an explicit field allowlist and avoids raw prompt, document or secret dumps in routine logs. Events include stage, timings, safe error category, candidate count, selected chunk/version identities, ranking movement, provider/model and fallback/cache state. Context/answer fingerprints aid repeated-question diagnosis without logging the full text. Raw source evidence remains in controlled artifacts rather than being copied into every log line."),
("16.3 Failure analysis", "For a failed question, first inspect whether any eligible indexed evidence existed. Then inspect query-embedding completion, candidate count, expected-chunk presence before and after reranking, final-context omission warnings, model status and citation-validation result. A model_declared_insufficient_evidence result with good candidates differs from no_candidates, no_complete_context_within_budget or provider_unavailable. A repeated question can differ because of source changes, rank movement, prompt budget, cache state or provider variability."),
("16.4 Performance cost of this increment", "Persistent chats add small PostgreSQL reads/writes; they add no embedding or rerank calls. Reopening history checks the thread's distinct evidence references in one batched approval/access query rather than opening a connection per quotation. Comparison expansion adds bounded local relational context lookup/access checks but no extra query embedding or reranking request. Added source context can increase generation prompt size, subject to the existing byte ceiling. Streaming changes delivery, not the number of normal provider requests; a normal streamed answer does not require an extra generation. It adds bounded per-claim access checks and checks queued output before transmission. It waits for a complete claim before displaying text, so it is not the same latency as unchecked first-token release. No new real-provider latency benchmark was run for this increment."),
("16.5 Resource planning", "Long layout/OCR conversions can take minutes on a local CPU and depend on image density and page complexity. Remote office compute should be requested as a secured workstation/VM with the actual parser dependencies, sufficient RAM/CPU, persistent storage and an approved access path; GPU value depends on the selected local layout/LLM stack. No hardware throughput guarantee is inferred from one PDF's elapsed time. Measure representative pages and separate extraction time from provider/network cooldowns."),
]),
("17. Testing, benchmarking and acceptance", [
("17.1 Unit and integration layers", "The tests cover paragraph/table FAQ parsing, source links, OCR and visual guards, damaged fonts/formulas, chunk metadata, review/index boundaries, worker recovery, provider transport/schema behaviour, source scoping, retrieval/rerank ordering, generation validation, schedule filtering and hosted isolation. Integration runs require an explicitly isolated gsme_rag_test database and uniquely scoped Qdrant collections. Fake embeddings/reranking are never described as a real Cohere quality evaluation."),
("17.2 Real-source versus synthetic tests", "Synthetic fixtures make failure cases reproducible without external calls or company-content disclosure. Real manual/validation source regressions compare known pages and regions where those files are available. Deleted optional bundled fixtures can be supplied through explicit test environment paths; a skipped source test is not a pass. A live provider benchmark separately requires content/call-limit approval and usable quota."),
("17.3 Positive and negative cases", "Positive cases should include tapeout postponement, commercial use, relative GDS deadlines, fabless ownership, actual fabless/IDM comparisons, manufacturing stages and PCM definitions. Near-topic negatives include an exact NDA monetary penalty absent from the source, invented tapeout guarantees, unsupported numerical specifications and unverified chart mappings. A search may legitimately return related chunks for a negative question; the failure is an unsupported answer, not simply a nonempty candidate list."),
("17.4 Metrics and labels", "Candidate recall measures whether source-labeled expected evidence entered the candidate set. Hit@k and MRR assess ranking. Final-context coverage checks whether all necessary facts survived budget/deduplication. Generation evaluation separately counts correct answers/abstentions, unsupported claims and contradictions using source-bound human judgments. Exact quote validity and an LLM's self-reported status are not automatically labeled semantic groundedness accuracy."),
("17.5 Calibration and repeatability", "Threshold calibration requires verified answerability labels, enough positive/negative groups, a tuning split and an independent held-out split. Variants of one question stay in the same group to prevent leakage. Benchmark outputs retain model, strategy, source version and rank traces so comparisons are interpretable. Repeating one successful question is useful diagnosis, but not a statistically sufficient quality certificate."),
("17.6 Current increment regressions", "New focused cases check chat ownership, persistence, rename/delete, stale-source masking and no body-selected ownership; cross-page comparison context with held/revoked/wrong-section exclusions; rejection of an introductory IDM citation; and explicit clarification for IDP. Browser automation exercises desktop collapse, independent saved chats, reload restoration, owner isolation, clickable sources, inline previews, mobile drawer and scroll/composer behaviour. The run results appear in the verification record below."),
]),
("18. Local runbook and demonstration", [
("18.1 Start the dependencies", "Start Docker Desktop first. From the repository, run docker compose -f compose.local.yaml up -d. A missing dockerDesktopLinuxEngine named pipe means the daemon is not running, not that the PDF is invalid. Check that PostgreSQL and Qdrant health/ports are available. A changed Compose password does not necessarily change the password inside an existing initialized PostgreSQL volume; restore the actual account configuration rather than deleting valuable volumes."),
("18.2 Start the chatbot", "Use .\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m gsme_rag.hosted.app and open http://127.0.0.1:8020. The launcher applies migrations and prints the log path. If WinError 10048 occurs, the port is already occupied; identify the process and reuse or stop the intended old server before starting another. Do not launch many copies and assume the browser is showing the newest code. Restart after code/configuration changes and refresh the page."),
("18.3 Open the operator backend", "Use .\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m gsme_rag.storage.admin for the local console on http://127.0.0.1:8010. It supports source/artifact inspection, review, indexing and retrieval diagnostics. Review authorization requires the configured reviewer and random local token. Do not put the admin token into public chatbot code or expose this loopback console on a company public URL. The parser/demo API is a separate entry point; its docs are not the hosted chatbot."),
("18.4 Demonstrate an uploaded FAQ", "Upload a small selectable-text FAQ document with the plus button. Observe processing and Ready to chat, choose the file or All files, ask a source-supported question, expand a citation and open the original. Ask a near-topic unsupported question and show a truthful abstention. Start a second chat, ask a different question, switch back and refresh to show persisted history. Collapse and reopen the sidebar without losing the conversation."),
("18.5 Demonstrate a complex manual safely", "Use the original MFG-GSME-0002.pdf, not an unverified generated excerpt. Ask what fabless means, whether a fabless company owns fabs, and the difference between fabless companies and IDMs. For the comparison, the expected source coverage is page 27's fabless definition and page 28's IDM definition. Show that uncertain table/formula/chart material remains held, not that it was silently guessed. Request details and logs should reveal exactly which evidence entered the answer."),
("18.6 Test commands and source fixtures", "The normal offline entry is .\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -B -m unittest discover -s tests. Set GSME_TEST_DATABASE_URL to an isolated gsme_rag_test* database and GSME_TEST_QDRANT_URL to the local test service for integration coverage. Set GSME_TEST_VALIDATION_PDF and GSME_TEST_MANUAL_PDF only to local source files when the relevant tests need them. tools/verify_hosted_ui.py --guest runs synthetic browser checks with the installed Playwright/Edge environment. No test command here authorizes new company-content API calls."),
]),
("19. Current incident resolution and handover", [
("19.1 Fabless/IDM incident", "The reported comparison failed because page 27's fabless text was approved/indexed while page 28's actual IDM definition was pending with no embedding job. The page 27 introductory sentence names two business models but does not state that IDMs own fabs. Inspection of the original and rendered pages confirmed the relevant definitions. Two ordinary page-28 prose chunks passed the existing automatic clean-text policy; no human verification flag was fabricated and the comparison table remains held."),
("19.2 Implemented correction", "Approved near-section context bridges the page break from a retrieved comparison anchor without embedding the whole manual again. Context retains page 27/page 28 identities and is distinguished from reranked hits. The answer guard rejects an IDM property supported only by an introductory name-list sentence. In the hosted chat, 'Fabless vs IDP' explicitly states the conditional IDM interpretation rather than claiming the acronyms are equivalent. A source-backed dry run using all four logged passages and a synthetic clarification response returned actual page 27/page 28 definitions, even with a whole-passage prompt-budget omission warning. This is not a new live Cohere quality result. The SDK's experimental-schema notice is not treated as the cause of the semantic clarification failure and is not hidden to make conversion appear successful."),
("19.3 What remains source/provider dependent", "The current turn does not prove that a future live Cohere ranking will always select the expected anchor or that every generated comparison will be correct. A fresh live end-to-end check needs available provider quota and approved bounded calls. General semantic entailment remains a source-review/evaluation task. The actual official Muse logo still needs a supplied asset. Existing user changes and the removed validation fixture have not been overwritten or restored by this increment."),
("19.4 Internship submission checklist", "Submit the maintained source, dependency configuration, schema migrations, this technical handover and an accurate demonstration. Keep .env, credentials, private originals, local databases, caches and oversized validation artifacts out of source control unless explicitly required. Record the exact code version and test results. State which optional adapters were tested synthetically versus with a real provider. Confirm deployment/authentication/retention decisions before labeling the hosted system company-production-ready."),
]),
]


def add_table(document, headings, rows):
    table = document.add_table(rows=1, cols=len(headings))
    table.style = "Light Shading Accent 1"
    for cell, heading in zip(table.rows[0].cells, headings):
        cell.text = heading
    for values in rows:
        for cell, value in zip(table.add_row().cells, values):
            cell.text = str(value)
    document.add_paragraph()


def build(output, verification):
    doc = Document()
    section = doc.sections[0]
    section.top_margin = section.bottom_margin = Inches(.75)
    section.left_margin = section.right_margin = Inches(.8)
    normal = doc.styles["Normal"]
    normal.font.name = "Calibri"
    normal.font.size = Pt(10.5)
    normal.paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(7)
    normal.paragraph_format.line_spacing = 1.12
    for name in ("Title", "Heading 1", "Heading 2"):
        doc.styles[name].font.color.rgb = RGBColor.from_string("176B56")
    section.header.paragraphs[0].text = "GSME MUSE  |  Technical implementation and handover"
    footer = section.footer.paragraphs[0]
    footer.alignment = WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.RIGHT
    footer.add_run("Project handover • Page ")
    field = OxmlElement("w:fldSimple"); field.set(qn("w:instr"), "PAGE")
    footer._p.append(field)

    doc.add_paragraph("GSME Muse", "Title")
    doc.add_paragraph("Complete Technical Implementation & Project Handover", "Subtitle")
    doc.add_paragraph("Parsing • Chunking • Evidence review • Embeddings • Storage\nHybrid retrieval • Reranking • Cited answers • Schedule search\nHosted chatbot • Multi-chat history • Testing • Operations")
    add_table(doc, ["Document control", "Value"], [
        ("Application version", __version__), ("Parser / chunker / retrieval versions", f"{PARSER_VERSION} / {CHUNKER_VERSION} / {RETRIEVAL_VERSION}"),
        ("Documentation date", "17 November 2026 (Asia/Karachi)"),
        ("Scope", "Checked-out local repository; not a production certification"),
        ("Data handling", "Contains architecture and source references; no API keys/passwords or full source-document dumps"),
        ("Current verification", verification),
    ])
    doc.add_paragraph("Readiness statement", "Heading 2")
    doc.add_paragraph("The implementation provides an evidence-controlled local RAG workflow. Its safeguards deliberately refuse unsupported answers. Production access configuration, provider capacity, representative source review and operational acceptance remain separate responsibilities. Optional adapters and historical live tests are not presented as newly verified production capabilities.")
    doc.add_page_break()
    doc.add_heading("Contents", 1)
    # A static contents list is immediately useful in viewers that do not update Word fields.
    for title, _ in SECTIONS:
        doc.add_paragraph(title)
    doc.add_paragraph("20. Verification record\nAppendix A. Module map\nAppendix B. Hosted API reference\nAppendix C. SQL migration inventory\nAppendix D. Configuration checklist\nAppendix E. Numerical defaults and limits\nAppendix F. Streaming event contract\nAppendix G. Demonstration script and question bank\nAppendix H. Replacing shared sources safely\nAppendix I. Version 0.19.9 source and security audit\nAppendix J. Version 0.19.10 admin workspace")

    for title, items in SECTIONS:
        doc.add_page_break()
        doc.add_heading(title, 1)
        for heading, paragraph in items:
            doc.add_heading(heading, 2)
            doc.add_paragraph(paragraph)

    doc.add_page_break()
    doc.add_heading("20. Verification record", 1)
    doc.add_paragraph(verification)
    add_table(doc, ["Verification type", "What the result establishes", "What it does not establish"], [
        ("Full local suite", "Regression behaviour under the recorded fixtures and isolated services", "Perfect retrieval on unseen files or real-provider accuracy"),
        ("Hosted browser checks", "Actual browser controls, history, scrolling, inline previews and isolation", "Real Google Workspace SSO or company hosting"),
        ("Original MFG pages 27–28", "Stored definitions compared with selectable text and rendered source pages", "Every formula, table and chart in the manual has been source-reviewed"),
        ("Source-backed protocol dry run", "Both actual definition passages can enter approved context with page identities", "A new live Cohere embedding/rerank/generation evaluation"),
        ("No new external model calls", "This increment did not consume company-content API test quota", "Current provider accounts have available quota"),
    ])

    doc.add_page_break()
    doc.add_heading("Appendix A. Module map", 1)
    modules = [
        ("parsing/parser.py", "Format dispatch, source digests, document/schedule metadata"),
        ("parsing/pdf.py", "Native text/layout extraction, page furniture, raster supplementation"),
        ("parsing/docling_pdf.py", "Optional structural conversion, dropped-table-cell capture and provenance"),
        ("parsing/ocr.py; parsing/image.py", "Tesseract discovery/English data and review-marked OCR"),
        ("parsing/fidelity.py; parsing/visual_review.py", "Damaged technical text and region/visual review"),
        ("parsing/docx.py; parsing/office.py; parsing/csv.py", "Word, slides, workbooks and CSV extraction"),
        ("parsing/markdown.py; parsing/links.py", "Control markers, normalization, tables and source hyperlink integrity"),
        ("chunking/chunker.py; chunking/semantic.py", "Structural evidence units and optional exact-text local boundaries"),
        ("models.py; review.py; indexing.py", "Contracts and independent evidence eligibility"),
        ("storage/postgres.py; storage/migrations", "Relational authority, versions, reviews, jobs and schema"),
        ("storage/pipeline.py; storage/files.py", "Leased parse/index processing and immutable file/artifact checks"),
        ("storage/providers.py; storage/vectors.py", "Embedding/transport adapters and derived vector/lexical index"),
        ("storage/acceptance.py", "Conservative automatic clean-text policy"),
        ("retrieval/service.py; retrieval/planning.py", "Scoped candidate search, fusion, reranking and bounded context"),
        ("retrieval/reranking.py", "Cross-encoder adapter and strict rank validation"),
        ("retrieval/schedules.py; parsing/schedules.py", "Typed schedule import, filters, dates and snapshots"),
        ("generation/answers.py; generation/gemini.py", "Primary/fallback answers, schema/citation validation and repeatability"),
        ("generation/compression.py", "Optional exact paragraph selection"),
        ("generation/streaming.py; hosted/streaming.py", "Incremental checked-claim parsing and bounded SSE/cancellation transport"),
        ("hosted/app.py; hosted/web", "Public chatbot API, upload scheduler and browser UX"),
        ("hosted/access.py; hosted/identity.py; hosted/sessions.py", "Tenant/owner policies, verified sign-in and browser workspaces"),
        ("hosted/history.py", "Persistent owner-only chat threads and stale-source masking"),
        ("observability.py", "Request correlation and content-safe structured stage logging"),
        ("retrieval/evaluation.py; retrieval/benchmarking.py; generation/evaluation.py", "Source-bound ranking, threshold and answer evaluation"),
        ("storage/admin.py; api/routes.py; cli.py", "Separate operator/demo/command-line entry points"),
    ]
    add_table(doc, ["Path below src/gsme_rag", "Responsibility"], modules)

    doc.add_heading("Appendix B. Hosted API reference", 1)
    tree = ast.parse((ROOT / "src/gsme_rag/hosted/app.py").read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    routes = []
    for node in ast.walk(tree):
        if not isinstance(node, (ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef)):
            continue
        for decorator in node.decorator_list:
            if (isinstance(decorator, ast.Call) and isinstance(decorator.func, ast.Attribute)
                    and isinstance(decorator.func.value, ast.Name) and decorator.func.value.id == "app"
                    and decorator.func.attr in {"get", "post", "patch", "delete"}
                    and decorator.args and isinstance(decorator.args[0], ast.Constant)):
                routes.append((decorator.func.attr.upper(), decorator.args[0].value, node.name))
    add_table(doc, ["Method", "Route", "Handler"], routes)
    doc.add_paragraph("Routes are extracted from the checked-out hosted app, not guessed from the operator console. Authentication/access/CSRF controls still apply. A chat_id is optional on POST /api/chat for backward compatibility; clients with a thread save only the server-produced response. Requests never accept a tenant or owner selector.")

    doc.add_heading("Appendix C. SQL migration inventory", 1)
    migrations = sorted((ROOT / "src/gsme_rag/storage/migrations").glob("[0-9][0-9][0-9]_*.sql"))
    add_table(doc, ["Migration", "Leading purpose/comment"], [(p.name, next((s[2:].strip() for s in p.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines() if s.startswith("--")), "See packaged SQL definition")) for p in migrations])
    doc.add_heading("Appendix D. Configuration checklist", 1)
    add_table(doc, ["Group", "Settings / checks"], [
        ("Local services", "GSME_DATABASE_URL, GSME_POSTGRES_PASSWORD, GSME_QDRANT_URL, GSME_DATA_DIR; never copy real values into this document"),
        ("Embedding", "GSME_EMBED_DIMENSION=1024, GSME_EMBED_BATCH=16, GSME_WORKER_BATCH=8, GSME_MAX_TOKENS=8192; COHERE_API_KEY and external-content approval required for real provider"),
        ("Reranking", "GSME_RERANK_MODEL, GSME_RERANK_TIMEOUT, GSME_RERANK_INPUT_BUDGET; separate GSME_RERANK_CONTENT_APPROVED"),
        ("Answers", "GSME_ANSWER_PROVIDER, GSME_ANSWER_MODEL, GSME_ANSWER_TIMEOUT, GSME_ANSWER_CONTENT_APPROVED, GSME_OLLAMA_MODEL"),
        ("Optional Gemini", "GEMINI_API_KEY, GSME_GEMINI_MODEL and GSME_GEMINI_CONTENT_APPROVED; answer-model choice does not migrate embeddings/reranking"),
        ("Parsing/chunking", "GSME_PDF_BACKEND and GSME_CHUNK_STRATEGY; Tesseract/English visibility; optional Docling and local semantic model digest"),
        ("Hosted access", "GSME_HOSTED_ORIGIN, GSME_HOSTED_TENANT, GSME_PUBLIC_FAQ_GUEST_ACCESS, GSME_GUEST_UPLOADS_ENABLED; optional Google OAuth/domain settings"),
        ("Limits", "GSME_CHAT_PER_USER_MINUTE, GSME_CHAT_GLOBAL_MINUTE, GSME_CHAT_GLOBAL_DAY, GSME_UPLOAD_GLOBAL_DAY; calibrated relevance gate only if justified"),
        ("Operator", "GSME_AUTHORIZED_REVIEWERS, random GSME_REVIEW_AUTH_TOKEN, GSME_LOG_LEVEL; keep the admin loopback-only"),
        ("Configuration hygiene", "Use one entry per key. Restart processes after changes. Keep real .env out of Git. Add only genuinely new settings at the end of .env.example."),
    ])
    doc.add_heading("Appendix E. Numerical defaults and limits", 1)
    add_table(doc, ["Control", "Current default / bound", "Meaning"], [
        ("Embedding", "Document: embed-v5.0-pro; query: embed-v5.0-fast; 1,024 dimensions", "search_document versus search_query; document-model changes need an index migration"),
        ("Embedding dimension choices", "256, 512, 768, 1,024, 1,536, 2,048", "Provider adapter validates supported dimensions; collection must match"),
        ("Normal chunk size", "1,800 characters", "Target; never silently truncate indivisible technical records"),
        ("Embedding tokens", "8,192", "Preflight budget, separate from chunk characters and prompt bytes"),
        ("Batches / worker lease", "16 embedding batch; 8 claimed jobs; 300-second lease", "Bound work and refresh leases during long operations"),
        ("Candidate / result counts", "30 / 5", "Up to 30 passages reranked; 5 final units, with separately labeled source context"),
        ("Retrieval context", "16,000 characters", "Whole evidence units omitted rather than truncated when over budget"),
        ("Relevance threshold", "Unset", "Requires verified tuning/held-out calibration; not a correctness probability"),
        ("Query variants", "Original by default; at most 3 with opt-in modes", "Hosted chat does not silently enable multi-query"),
        ("Rerank model / timeout", "rerank-v5.0-pro / 30 seconds", "Mandatory before generation; fast model also supported by validation"),
        ("Rerank input guard", "8,192 UTF-8 bytes including question/framing allowance", "Conservative per-question/passage check, not evidence truncation"),
        ("Answer prompt / output", "6,000 bytes / 1,024 output tokens", "Model-specific reasoning allowance is separately controlled where implemented"),
        ("Answer timeout", "60 seconds", "Applies to configured primary/local provider operation"),
        ("Answer cache", "120 seconds, 64 entries, 2,000,000 bytes", "Process-local validated primary output only; source/access rechecks mandatory"),
        ("Tokenizer cache", "128 exact successful entries", "Credential/model/text-hash namespace; no estimated token counts"),
        ("Comparison expansion", "At most 3 prose siblings; ±6 chunk indices; ±1 source page", "Same approved comparison heading/version/category; no held tables or OCR"),
        ("Upload / concurrency", "20 MiB; 4 upload slots; 2 chat slots", "Limits are not a production throughput SLA"),
        ("Background scheduler", "2-second poll", "Durable next-attempt timestamps control provider cooldowns"),
        ("Default public request caps", "6 chats/user/minute; 8 global/minute; 50 global/day; 30 uploads/day", "Environment-configurable within validated bounds"),
        ("Browser workspace access", "7 days", "Cookie expiry loses access, not automatic file erasure"),
        ("Chat history limits", "100 threads/owner; 100 turns/thread", "Owner scoped; delete a thread to remove its stored turns"),
        ("Local ports", "8020 chatbot; 8010 operator; 5432 PostgreSQL; 6333 Qdrant", "Parser/demo API is separate; do not publicly expose operator or database ports"),
    ])
    doc.add_heading("Appendix F. Streaming event contract", 1)
    doc.add_paragraph("POST /api/chat/stream accepts the same question, optional document_id/chat_id and generation flag as POST /api/chat. It uses the same owner/access/approval boundary. The original JSON endpoint remains available. SSE HTTP headers indicate transport acceptance; a later error event is still a failed request, not a successful answer.")
    add_table(doc, ["Event", "Payload / behaviour"], [
        ("status", "Search/generation stage, optional explicitly disclosed query interpretation, provider/fallback state; no raw reasoning"),
        ("claim", "Sequential index, checked complete claim text and source references. Provisional until the done event; at most eight model claims"),
        ("reset", "Discard provisional primary-provider claims before an operational fallback starts"),
        ("done", "Final server-built answer/result with validated citations and diagnostics; only finalized server output is saved to history"),
        ("error", "Safe detail/code/request ID; remove unfinished output and show the operational problem without raw provider payloads"),
        ("comment", "A transport keep-alive, not answer text"),
    ])
    doc.add_paragraph("The transport queue is bounded to 24 events, the application permits two active streaming workers, and raw answer accumulation is capped at 128,000 UTF-8 bytes. JSON parsing uses an actual decoder, including escape handling and duplicate-key rejection. On disconnect the worker is notified, and cancellation is checked before further output or turn persistence. In-flight blocking SDK reads cannot be forcibly killed; normal provider timeouts remain relevant. Reference: Google Gemini generate-content/streamGenerateContent protocol, https://ai.google.dev/api/generate-content?hl=en. Cohere streaming fields were also checked against the installed SDK types.")
    doc.add_page_break()
    doc.add_heading("Appendix G. Complete screen demonstration and question bank", 1)
    doc.add_paragraph("Demonstration target: the local chatbot at http://127.0.0.1:8020. Allow about 10–12 minutes. This is a read-and-click script, not a claim that live provider calls were rerun for this documentation update. Rehearse once with your current credentials/quota. Do not show .env, API keys, database passwords or unrelated private files on screen.")
    demo = [
        ("Before recording — start and verify", "Start Docker Desktop, then run docker compose -f compose.local.yaml up -d from the repository. Start .\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m gsme_rag.hosted.app in a second terminal. Open http://127.0.0.1:8020 and refresh after restarting an older server. Check that the FAQ files and MFG-GSME-0002.pdf are available. If a provider is exhausted or unavailable, resolve that before recording; do not present a quota error as a retrieval-quality failure. Correction: although the local environment has GSME_HYBRID=false, hosted app.backend explicitly constructs hybrid=True and hosted RetrievalOptions defaults to hybrid. The chatbot therefore combines dense vectors and BM25 with reciprocal-rank fusion before reranking. The environment flag affects other entry points and does not disable this hosted path. The local Qdrant text index was verified to use BM25. Show the actual answer provider/model in Request details rather than claiming Gemini is active."),
        ("Before recording — make schedules available", "The user's exact full_schedules.csv (33 rows) and shared_schedules.csv (14 rows) were published in local-test on 17 November 2026. Guest-access schedule search verifies 47 records across these two sources. Do not upload the old workbook as an additional source for this demonstration: overlapping sources are retained separately and can duplicate results. These CSV schedule records are shared; original CSV download remains private under the existing schedule publication policy. The older stored workbook still has no hosted publication policy. File edits on disk are not automatically watched or imported."),
        ("00:00 — introduction", "SHOW: Chat landing screen, sidebar and Chat / Tapeout schedules switch. SAY: This is GSME Muse, a source-grounded assistant for FAQs, manufacturing documents and tapeout schedules. It supports both natural-language document questions and exact schedule-record searches. The two modes are explicit because a deadline policy question is different from a request for a calendar date."),
        ("00:45 — FAQ retrieval and citations", "CLICK: Chat; leave Search in set to All files. ASK: When was Muse founded? EXPECT: February 2018, supported by the FAQ source. SAY: The app searches the accepted current document collection, reranks candidate passages and generates an answer with references. CLICK an E reference to expand its supporting extract, then Open document to view the source. Explain that E1 is an evidence reference, not a confidence score."),
        ("01:45 — semantic paraphrases", "ASK: What should I do if my tapeout must be postponed? EXPECT: reschedule or cancel by email without charge before the Final GDS deadline. ASK: How many days before tapeout are preliminary and final GDS uploads due? EXPECT: preliminary 14 days; final 7 days; the FAQ states the same deadlines for Full and Shared. SAY: Different wording can retrieve the same FAQ evidence. These are general source policies, not computed schedule dates."),
        ("02:45 — complex document", "SELECT: MFG-GSME-0002.pdf in Search in to demonstrate narrowing. ASK: What are the three main semiconductor manufacturing stages? EXPECT: fabrication, assembly and testing, supported by page 18. ASK: What is the difference between fabless companies and IDMs? EXPECT: fabless outsources fabrication; IDM covers design and manufacturing, using the source definitions on pages 27–28. Open the supporting pages. Do not treat a heading mentioning both models as proof of the full comparison."),
        ("04:00 — safe refusal", "RETURN Search in to All files. ASK: What exact monetary penalty does Muse charge for breaching its NDA? EXPECT: no unsupported monetary amount; the FAQ discusses required agreements but does not state an exact breach penalty. SAY: Related chunks are not sufficient evidence for an invented number. If search matches are displayed, they are explicitly not cited as an answer. This is an intended refusal, not a failure to respond."),
        ("04:45 — exact schedules", "CLICK Tapeout schedules. Keep Schedule set to From my question and date filters empty. ASK: Show both schedules. With only the two intended shared CSV sources accessible, EXPECT: 47 records: 33 Full and 14 Shared. The table shows technology, flavor, trial/final deadlines, tapeout/shipment dates and source file/row. Open source is offered only when original-file permission exists; publishing schedule rows does not publish the whole CSV. SAY: This uses typed database records, not vector similarity or an LLM-generated date. Imported rows are not live foundry capacity."),
        ("05:45 — schedule filtering", "ASK: Show shared 28nm schedules flavor \"HPC+ RF\" between 2026-11-01 and 2026-12-31. EXPECT two tapeout dates in this workbook: 2026-11-11 and 2026-12-09, with final deadlines 2026-11-04 and 2026-12-02. Use the optional date filters to demonstrate explicit milestone selection, then clear them. Explain that exact flavor spelling is intentional and contradictory filters request clarification."),
        ("06:45 — schedule boundaries", "ASK: List tapeout dates. With no Schedule menu choice, EXPECT clarification to select Full, Shared or both. ASK: Show full 3nm schedules. EXPECT no matching records, not an invented date. Optionally ASK Next 3 full tapeout dates: as of 2026-11-17 Asia/Karachi, the original workbook gives three distinct dates (2026-11-18, 2026-12-01, 2026-12-02) across six rows. Explain that ties are retained and relative results change with the date."),
        ("07:45 — uploads and source quality", "CLICK + to show file upload; if needed upload an approved, small selectable-text FAQ file not an unrelated private document. SHOW automatic processing status, then Ready to chat. SAY: Parsing normalizes supported documents, chunks them structurally, preserves source locations and holds uncertain OCR, tables, formulas and chart claims for review. Accepted passages are embedded and indexed. A held passage is not automatically verified just to make ingestion finish. Do not start a long manual upload during the recording unless its processing time is part of the demonstration."),
        ("08:45 — usability", "RETURN Chat, click New chat, ask one short question, rename the saved conversation and reopen an older chat. Collapse and restore the sidebar. Show Enter to send and Shift+Enter for a new line. Explain that saved conversations are owner-scoped history: each question still performs its own fresh search; follow-up pronouns are not promised conversational memory. Schedule lookups are currently not stored as chat turns."),
        ("09:30 — technical inspection", "EXPAND Request details on a document answer. SHOW actual passages reranked, provider/model, request ID and any fallback state; do not claim a hardcoded provider was used. SAY: The usual retrieval configuration collects up to 30 candidates and returns five evidence units after reranking; the actual count can be lower. Approved comparison context can be added separately. Embeddings are in Qdrant; authoritative sources, versions, review state, jobs, schedules and history are in PostgreSQL; originals and normalized artifacts are on disk. The local operator console is separate on port 8010 and must not be exposed publicly."),
        ("10:30 — logs and conclusion", "SHOW the server terminal briefly. Correlate a request ID with retrieval, reranking and answer-stage events or data/logs/console.log. Never show secrets. SAY: The implementation covers ingestion through cited answers and exact schedules, with source provenance, access controls, streaming and regression tests. Current provider quota, source approval, intended publication policy and hosted deployment settings must still be checked for a real release. No automatic safeguard proves that every generated sentence is semantically correct; citations remain inspectable."),
    ]
    for title, content in demo:
        doc.add_heading(title, 2)
        doc.add_paragraph(content)
    doc.add_heading("G.1 Semantic search practice questions", 2)
    add_table(doc, ["Question", "Source-backed target / acceptance"], [
        ("When was Muse founded?", "FAQs QA Format.docx, General 07: February 2018."),
        ("Can a commercial company use Muse services?", "General 03: yes; exact source wording should be cited."),
        ("Who should I contact for commercial questions and technical support?", "General 01: sales@musesemi.com versus support@musesemi.com."),
        ("What if I need to reschedule or cancel my tapeout?", "TapeOut Services 03: email without charge before Final GDS deadline."),
        ("What are the preliminary and final GDS upload deadlines?", "TapeOut Services 02: 14 and 7 days before tapeout, same for Full/Shared."),
        ("How does Shared Block work, and must I coordinate with other customers?", "Shared Block 01/03: aggregates projects; Muse handles aggregation; customer submits its individual project."),
        ("What are the three main semiconductor manufacturing stages?", "MFG-GSME-0002.pdf page 18: fabrication, assembly and testing."),
        ("How do fabless companies differ from IDMs?", "MFG-GSME-0002.pdf pages 27–28: compare actual definitions, not only the introductory heading."),
        ("What exact monetary NDA breach penalty does Muse charge?", "Near-topic negative: no exact penalty amount in the inspected FAQ. Do not invent one."),
        ("What exact date in February 2018 was Muse founded?", "Near-topic negative/partial: inspected FAQ gives month/year only, not day."),
        ("What guaranteed percentage yield will my next Shared Block tapeout achieve?", "Near-topic negative: a service explanation is not a project-specific yield guarantee."),
    ])
    doc.add_heading("G.2 Exact schedule practice questions", 2)
    add_table(doc, ["Question / settings", "Expected behaviour for the original 47-row workbook"], [
        ("Show both schedules", "47 rows if that workbook is accessible and uploaded once; 33 Full / 14 Shared. Additional accessible sources may change totals."),
        ('Show shared 28nm schedules flavor "HPC+ RF" between 2026-11-01 and 2026-12-31', "Two rows: tapeout 2026-11-11 / 2026-12-09. Compare source sheet and row before reporting."),
        ("Show shared final deadlines before 2026-11-01", "Seven rows in this workbook; filter applies to final_deadline, not tapeout_date."),
        ("Next 3 full tapeout dates", "As of 2026-11-17: six rows on three distinct dates. A later run may legitimately differ."),
        ("Show full 3nm schedules", "No matching rows in the workbook. Never invent an alternative date."),
        ("List tapeout dates; Schedule menu = From my question", "Ask Full, Shared or both; do not silently broaden."),
        ("Show shared schedules; Schedule menu = Full", "Conflicting schedule_kind clarification; do not ignore either constraint."),
        ("Show shared schedules; From later than Through", "Validation error; do not silently swap dates."),
    ])
    doc.add_paragraph("Verification distinction: the earlier workbook SHA-256 and all 47 parsed rows were checked against stored values. The user's two CSVs are now the shared sources: Full document e887637c-7687-4eaa-b12f-15664beb5210 and Shared document c93b8c93-35e6-4bf5-a37e-e805fd13d001. Source hashes, all typed values and row identities are checked on ingestion. This is not confirmation that the publisher's dates remain current. FAQ targets were checked in the stored original Word document; manual source anchors refer to the PDF inspection recorded elsewhere in this handover.")
    doc.add_heading("Appendix H. Replacing these shared sources safely", 1)
    doc.add_paragraph("A filename is not a document identity. Editing the file on disk does nothing to the saved original. Uploading through + creates a new owner-only document; it does not replace a shared-library file, even with the same name. An operator must submit the replacement using the same logical document_id, ingest it, check its results and explicitly publish the new exact version to the shared library. Prior versions remain for provenance but are superseded for current search. Identical bytes with the same parser/chunker/profile on that logical document are a no-op. Changing extraction settings can require a new version even for identical bytes.")
    doc.add_paragraph("Full CSV logical document: e887637c-7687-4eaa-b12f-15664beb5210. Shared CSV logical document: c93b8c93-35e6-4bf5-a37e-e805fd13d001. Manufacturing PDF logical document: d8117236-c045-4345-a682-10007f5237ba. Do not paste a version_id into --document-id.")
    doc.add_paragraph("Operator interface: start .\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m gsme_rag.storage.admin and open http://127.0.0.1:8010/admin. Connect using the local operator token and local-test workspace. Inspect the existing logical document and click Update selected document to fill its Existing document ID. Choose the replacement file and Full/Shared kind when appropriate, then Ingest document. For a PDF, authorize external embedding only for permitted content and wait for indexing. Inspect the new version, expand Shared-library publication, explicitly confirm all-reader access and click Publish shared version. This checks the exact current version and shares schedule records or the accepted document and original as applicable. Ordinary ingestion alone does not make a new version public. The CLI below remains an alternative, not a required extra UI step.")
    doc.add_paragraph('Example Full replacement, from the repository terminal: .\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m gsme_rag.storage.cli submit "D:\\Desktop\\GSME\\faq test files\\full_schedules.csv" --tenant local-test --document-id e887637c-7687-4eaa-b12f-15664beb5210 --schedule-kind full')
    doc.add_paragraph("Copy the returned job_id and version_id. Parse locally with: .\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m gsme_rag.storage.cli worker-once --tenant local-test --job-id NEW_JOB_ID --ingestion-only. Inspect the source and typed rows before publishing.")
    doc.add_paragraph("Publish the exact CSV version to shared search with: .\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe tools/publish_hosted_source.py --tenant local-test --document-id e887637c-7687-4eaa-b12f-15664beb5210 --version-id NEW_VERSION_ID --kind schedule --confirm-public. This prompts for the local operator token, which must be configured securely. Shared CSV uses its own logical ID and --schedule-kind shared. Do not run the publication command if submit returned a no-op for an already current version.")
    doc.add_paragraph("Schedule ingestion moves the current pointer before shared publication is rebound to the new exact version, so there can be a temporary shared-search gap until the operator republishes. This is not a zero-downtime promotion workflow. Failed parsing leaves the old current pointer untouched. PDF replacement similarly needs fresh acceptance, indexing and shared publication. Old vector points are denied by current-version/access checks and may be physically cleaned later; identical stored embeddings can be reused only when tenant/model/text checks pass. Schedule records do not need embeddings or Cohere calls.")
    doc.add_paragraph("Manufacturing ingestion baseline: the exact user-supplied PDF has 188 pages, source SHA-256 93c1780a3908b40da428233607599d539312497503b723d09e66bf645e84a621, and parsed through pymupdf_table_fallback in approximately 63.5 seconds. Docling was deliberately skipped for this large PDF; this is not a Docling validation. Of 802 extracted units, 218 clean-text sections were policy-accepted, 387 remain pending and 197 were excluded (including 188 generic visual-gap units). Accepted chunks start on 95 pages; this is not complete source coverage or human verification of 95 whole pages. All 157 extracted table-row units remain pending/review-required. Full PDF source-fidelity and retrieval/answer quality evaluation remains separate from successful indexing.")
    doc.add_heading("Appendix I. Version 0.19.9 source and security audit", 1)
    doc.add_paragraph("Fixed a confirmed single-kind XLSX ingestion defect: explicit Full/Shared kind is now allowed for workbooks as well as CSV. Office ZIP containers are checked before early spreadsheet classification and parsing: maximum 10,000 entries, 128 MiB expanded total and 64 MiB per entry; unsafe/duplicate/encrypted entries are rejected. This is a bounded-container safeguard, not an OS-level sandbox for arbitrary PDF/Office parsers.")
    doc.add_paragraph("A local fidelity diagnostic falsely treated the exact TSMC acronym definition as a mathematical expression. Diagnostics now mask only verified matching acronym initials in a comparison copy. Evidence text is unchanged; mismatched expansions, damaged Unicode and genuine equations still require review. The 188-page source was rerun natively using parser 0.18.2 in 85.648 seconds: 802 units, 544 review-marked, 197 excluded, no units over 1,800 characters. A separate automatic-policy calculation finds 220 eligible sections beginning on 96 pages. This is a local audit result, NOT the production index: the shared stored version still has 218 indexed passages starting on 95 pages. No document re-embedding was authorized or performed in this audit.")
    doc.add_paragraph("Rendered source comparisons: page 12 has three correctly extracted run/timeline pairs (MPW 8–14 weeks after tape-in, Engineering Run 6–8 weeks after tape-in, Mass Production Run 8–10 weeks optimized), still held as inferred table rows. Page 29 is a merged Cp/Cpk comparison table: extracted text is held because column meaning needs verification. Page 35 has a selectable OSAT title but its expansion/diagram is raster content; OCR is noisy and remains held. Page 6 contains the exact TSMC expansion plus decorative background/logo imagery. Generic visual-gap placeholders are excluded, not embedded. These checks are not verification of all 188 pages.")
    doc.add_paragraph("Security dependency review updated OpenTelemetry API to 1.45.2, SoupSieve to 4.0 and pip to 26.3. pip check found no broken requirements and the subsequent advisory scan found no known vulnerabilities. Static analysis reported 14 findings requiring contextual assessment: nine SQL construction sites use server-defined clauses or allowlisted identifiers and bound values; the legacy parser demo binds publicly and must not be exposed without deployment controls; Tesseract uses argument lists and timeouts, not a shell. Cleanup exception handling and subprocess-import notices were reviewed rather than suppressed. These checks do not certify an internet production deployment.")
    doc.add_paragraph("The bounded live evaluation reuses current document embeddings, separates dense and hybrid ranks, retains operational failures, and tests 12 accepted-source positives, four known held-coverage questions and four near-topic unsupported questions. Candidate rank, reranked rank, top-five presence, source IDs and final responses are retained in validation/audit-0.19.9/retrieval-live.json. A provider rate-limit failure is not a retrieval-quality miss and is not erased when the run resumes. See the verification record for the final actual results; neither model self-assessment nor candidate presence alone establishes groundedness.")
    doc.add_paragraph("Completed live pilot: 102/200 Cohere HTTP attempts, 40/40 search attempts and 20/20 Command answers; no document re-embedding. One dense search failed with HTTP 429 and remains recorded. After the approved cooldown, reranks were paced at least 15.2 seconds apart. Hybrid positive-case hit@1 = 10/12 and hit@5 = 12/12; MRR = 0.917. Dense on its 11 successful positive searches: hit@1 = 9/11, hit@5 = 11/11, MRR = 0.909; the twelfth attempt was operationally unavailable, not silently dropped from the report. This small source-pinned sample does not establish hybrid superiority or corpus-wide recall.")
    doc.add_paragraph("Reranker comparison on those same successful positives: hybrid expected-anchor MRR improved from 0.854 before reranking to 0.917 afterward, improving two expected ranks and worsening none. Dense improved from 0.894 to 0.909, improving one expected rank and worsening none. These labels identify expected source-anchor chunks, not exhaustive graded relevance judgments across all candidates. The 20 answer-stage durations ranged from 2.371 to 4.471 seconds; they exclude retrieval and the deliberate provider pacing, so they are not end-to-end latency or a company-load SLA. The local exact-source schedule audit passed 44/44 checks as of 2026-11-17 in 2.509 seconds, including its isolated ingestion and queries, with zero external calls.")
    doc.add_paragraph("All four near-topic negatives abstained, as did all four known held-coverage questions. The latter are safe failures to answer available PDF content, not complete document coverage. Review of the generated answers found one confirmed scope error: A09 attributed general wafer die-sorting outputs to parametric testing. The original answer is preserved as a failure. A local source-scope guard and regression now reject that specific misattribution, and the generation instruction preserves requested test subtypes. No additional live answer was sent after the 20-answer ceiling; this fix is locally verified, not live-retested. A07 also expands source 'ring oscillators' to 'ring oscillator frequency'; the cited excerpt does not explicitly state that qualifier. Treat that extra wording as a source-fidelity concern rather than claiming all positive answers are perfectly grounded. Exact quote validation is not general semantic entailment.")
    doc.add_heading("Appendix J. Version 0.19.10 admin workspace", 1)
    doc.add_paragraph("The local admin portal at http://127.0.0.1:8010/admin now has task-based sidebar navigation, a searchable document-card library and readable status summaries. Connect using the local operator token; processing mode remains visible so synthetic demo vectors cannot be mistaken for real Cohere embeddings. The token is not persisted in browser storage. FastAPI documentation is linked in the sidebar at /docs; protected requests use the X-GSME-Token header. This is not a publicly hosted administrator account system.")
    add_table(doc, ["Task", "Simplified workflow", "Boundary"], [
        ("Add a document", "Documents → Add document → choose file/type → authorize permitted external processing → Ingest", "Routine parsing/clean-text indexing uses the existing pipeline; no new approval bypass."),
        ("Update an existing source", "Click Update on its card, choose replacement, ingest, inspect and explicitly republish its shared version", "Preserves logical document ID. Old originals remain; ordinary new upload is not replacement."),
        ("Review held evidence", "Source review defaults to Needs review. Filter by source page and compare against local original preview", "Filters are applied by PostgreSQL before pagination. Summary counts cover the full document."),
        ("Review a page/table group", "Select displayed held passages, record one source-comparison note, confirm every selection, then approve/reject", "Shortcuts skip missing-link answers and do not select unseen rows. Each selected chunk gets its own persisted decision."),
        ("Check processing", "Jobs & logs → refresh → read reason → Open document or Retry local parsing", "Refresh is read-only. Local parse retry does not authorize external embedding or silently approve evidence."),
        ("Check retrieval", "Test search → question → optional strategy/candidate settings → authorize provider → Search & rerank", "Shows evidence and before/after ranks; generated answers remain in the chatbot. Scores are not confidence."),
        ("Check schedules", "Schedules → Full/Shared and exact filters → Find schedule rows", "Typed local database rows, not generated dates. Raw result retains source provenance."),
    ])
    doc.add_paragraph("PDF originals are rendered locally into a source-page image beside the extracted text, avoiding browser PDF-plugin dependence. The authenticated, tenant-scoped preview endpoint verifies the original SHA-256 and page bounds, rejects unsupported/corrupt/encrypted sources, bounds the bitmap to approximately four million pixels and returns no-store provenance headers. This rendering does not run OCR or a model and writes no cached source copies. Supported raster images can also be previewed; Office originals use an explicit download fallback because the browser does not natively render Word/Excel/PowerPoint. Source HTML/SVG/Office data is never inserted as executable markup. Open original in a new tab keeps the selected PDF page for native zoom. Source previews and blob URLs clear when the version/workspace changes. Review shows 25 passages per batch, or up to 100 when a source-page filter is selected, so most intact page/table groups can be checked together. Shortcuts still select displayed evidence only. Selections and their verification checkbox reset when filters, pagination or source scope changes. Fine-grained provenance, review authorization and separate public sharing remain enforced by the existing server boundaries.")
    doc.add_paragraph("Queue data is bounded and tenant-scoped. It distinguishes parsing from version/index status, retains stored failure information, and shows enrolled automatic processing and due timestamps without promising that a provider outage or quota limit is already resolved. Counts in the queue cover all model versions and are labelled accordingly; selected-mode index details remain in Source review. Low-level IDs, raw JSON, individual passage overrides, old versions and index maintenance are available in collapsed details instead of competing with everyday actions.")
    doc.core_properties.title = "GSME Muse — Complete Technical Implementation and Handover"
    doc.core_properties.subject = "Source-backed implementation, testing and operational limitations"
    doc.core_properties.author = "GSME Muse project"
    doc.core_properties.version = __version__
    doc.save(output)
